    detailedAnswer: "**Direct answer:**\n\nThis is a single linear scan: track the best value seen so far and its index, updating whenever a strictly larger value is found. The important edge cases to mention out loud in an interview are an empty list (should raise or return a sentinel, depending on the contract) and ties (the code below returns the first occurrence of the max, which should be stated explicitly since \"the index of the maximum\" is ambiguous when the max value repeats).\n\n**Example:**\n\n```python\ndef argmax(values):\n    if not values:\n        raise ValueError(\"empty input\")\n    best_idx = 0\n    best_val = values[0]\n    for i, v in enumerate(values):\n        if v > best_val:\n            best_val, best_idx = v, i\n    return best_idx\n```",
