    sampleAnswer: "Resist jumping straight to a specific model. Start by clarifying what \"cost\" actually means here (agent headcount hours, average handle time, ticket volume) and what data exists to support any proposed solution (historical tickets, resolution outcomes, agent notes). Lay out a few concrete, scoped options rather than a vague \"use AI\" answer ? for example: a classification model to route tickets to the right team automatically, a retrieval-based system to surface likely answers to agents (or directly to customers) from a knowledge base, or a model predicting which tickets are likely to escalate so they can be prioritized. For each option, briefly note the data needed, the expected impact mechanism, and a way to measure whether it actually worked once deployed, since a case-study answer that ends at \"and then we deploy the model\" without a measurement plan is usually seen as incomplete.",
    detailedAnswer: "**Direct answer:**\n\nResist jumping straight to a specific model. Start by clarifying what \"cost\" actually means here (agent headcount hours, average handle time, ticket volume) and what data exists to support any proposed solution (historical tickets, resolution outcomes, agent notes). Lay out a few concrete, scoped options rather than a vague \"use AI\" answer ? for example: a classification model to route tickets to the right team automatically, a retrieval-based system to surface likely answers to agents (or directly to customers) from a knowledge base, or a model predicting which tickets are likely to escalate so they can be prioritized. For each option, briefly note the data needed, the expected impact mechanism, and a way to measure whether it actually worked once deployed, since a case-study answer that ends at \"and then we deploy the model\" without a measurement plan is usually seen as incomplete.\n\n**Example:**\n\n\"I'd start with ticket auto-routing since it's lower risk than fully automating responses, requires only historical ticket-to-team labels we likely already have, and its impact ? reduced average handle time from fewer misrouted tickets ? is directly measurable within a few weeks of rollout, before considering something higher-risk like automated response drafting.\"\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\nCODING PRACTICE COMMONLY SEEN IN DATA SCIENCE INTERVIEWS\n\n",
